## Why This Is Asked

Quicksort with many duplicates can degrade; 3-way partitioning reduces swaps and comparisons.

## Key Concepts

- 3-way partitioning (Dutch National Flag)
- In-place iterative sorting (no recursion)
- Median-of-three pivot to avoid degeneracy
- Space: O(log n) for manual stack

## Code Example

```javascript
function quicksort3WayIterative(arr) {
  const stack = [];
  stack.push([0, arr.length - 1]);
  while (stack.length) {
    const [l, r] = stack.pop();
    if (l >= r) continue;
    const m = l + Math.floor((r - l) / 2);
    // median-of-three to pick pivot
    if (arr[l] > arr[m]) [arr[l], arr[m]] = [arr[m], arr[l]];
    if (arr[l] > arr[r]) [arr[l], arr[r]] = [arr[r], arr[l]];
    if (arr[m] > arr[r]) [arr[m], arr[r]] = [arr[r], arr[m]];
    const pivot = arr[m];
    // Dutch National Flag partition
    let i = l, lt = l, gt = r;
    while (i <= gt) {
      if (arr[i] < pivot) { [arr[lt], arr[i]] = [arr[i], arr[lt]]; lt++; i++; }
      else if (arr[i] > pivot) { [arr[i], arr[gt]] = [arr[gt], arr[i]]; gt--; }
      else { i++; }
    }
    stack.push([l, lt - 1]);
    stack.push([gt + 1, r]);
  }
}
``` 

